          "type": "graph",
          "say": "Thread one writes the data, then sets a ready flag. Thread two waits for the flag, then reads the data. But the compiler or the CPU may reorder thread one's writes, because within one thread nobody can tell the difference. Thread two sees ready, and reads stale data. The fix: store the flag with release, and load it with acquire. Everything written before the release is then visible after the acquire that reads it.",
